# generated native folders
/ios
/android

# Local Expo modules ship their own native SOURCE, which is not prebuild output.
#
# The repo-root .gitignore excludes `ios/` and `android/` WITHOUT a leading
# slash, so those patterns match a directory of that name at any depth — which
# silently swallowed modules/*/ios and modules/*/android. The files existed
# locally (so autolinking resolved them and everything looked fine) but were
# never uploaded to EAS, so the pod was never installed and the native module
# was never registered. On device that presented as the share extension saving a
# link the app could then never read.
#
# The two anchored patterns above still ignore the real prebuild output at
# mobile/ios and mobile/android. This file is lower in the tree than the root
# one, so these negations take precedence for anything under mobile/.
!modules/**/ios/
!modules/**/ios/**
!modules/**/android/
!modules/**/android/**

# Expo log
expo.log

